cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tacqor or cite its design, please cite the whitepaper as below."
title: "Tacqor: A Statically Typed Language with Python's Syntax and Native Speed"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Tacqor Authors"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tacqor/tacqor"
url: "https://tacqor.github.io/tacqor/"
abstract: "Tacqor is a general-purpose programming language that combines the readability of Python, the static guarantees of a Rust-style type system and error model, and native execution speed. A single executable checks, tests, compiles, packages and runs programs on a bytecode virtual machine or as machine code produced through the system C++ compiler, with identical semantics on both paths."
keywords:
  - programming language
  - compiler
  - virtual machine
  - static typing
  - Option and Result types
preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: "Tacqor: A Statically Typed Language with Python's Syntax and Native Speed (Whitepaper, version 1.2)"
  authors:
